                "Manual red-teaming—where human security researchers sit before a prompt interface and attempt to provoke policy violations—is essential but inherently unscalable. Human researchers suffer from cognitive fatigue, personal stylistic blindspots, and an inability to explore millions of combinatorial prompt variations. To achieve comprehensive safety attestation before deploying frontier models, organizations employ Automated Red-Teaming (ART) and Evolutionary Fuzzing engines. These systems treat red-teaming as a guided optimization problem, using an attacker LLM or evolutionary algorithm to search the prompt space for inputs that maximize the probability of safety policy failure in the target model.",
